<article class="env-definition" id="0348">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0348">Definition <span data-tag="0348">35.15.1</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{P}$ be a property of schemes. Let $\tau \in \{ fpqc, \linebreak[0] fppf, \linebreak[0] syntomic, \linebreak[0] smooth, \linebreak[0] {\acute{e}tale}, \linebreak[0] Zariski\} $. We say $\mathcal{P}$ is <em>local in the $\tau $-topology</em> if for any $\tau $-covering $\{ S_ i \to S\} _{i \in I}$ (see Topologies, Section <a href="/tag/020M" data-tag="020M">34.2</a>) we have </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  S \text{ has }\mathcal{P} \Leftrightarrow \text{each }S_ i \text{ has }\mathcal{P}.  \]
</div>
</article>